Subject: [PATCH 5/5] libtimedate-perl: upgrade 2.30 -> 2.35
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:33:02 -0800
Message-ID: <20261113003302.20809-6-tim.orling@konsulko.com>
X-Mailer: git-send-email 2.56.0
In-Reply-To: <20261113003302.20809-1-tim.orling@konsulko.com>
References: <20261113003302.20809-1-tim.orling@konsulko.com>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
List-Id: <openembedded-core.lists.openembedded.org>
X-Webhook-Received: from 45-33-107-173.ip.linodeusercontent.com [45.33.107.173] by lin-tor-korg-lkml-alma10-1 with HTTPS for <openembedded-core@lists.openembedded.org>; Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:33:36 -0000
X-Groupsio-URL: https://lists.openembedded.org/g/openembedded-core/message/250137
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"

AUH missed this upgrade because TimeDate is now released by ATOOMIC
and GBARR's directory stops at 2.30; update SRC_URI accordingly.

The license text moved from README to LICENSE; the terms are unchanged.
Add POSIX to RDEPENDS, and to the ptest RDEPENDS the modules the new
tests use, including tzdata-core so t/gh10 can use America/Los_Angeles.

Changes: https://metacpan.org/dist/TimeDate/changes

Tested by building target and native and running ptest on qemux86-64.

AI-Generated: Uses Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5)
Signed-off-by: Tim Orling <tim.orling@konsulko.com>
---
 ...-perl_2.30.bb => libtimedate-perl_2.35.bb} | 31 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 rename meta/recipes-extended/perl/{libtimedate-perl_2.30.bb => libtimedate-perl_2.35.bb} (31%)

diff --git a/meta/recipes-extended/perl/libtimedate-perl_2.30.bb b/meta/recipes-extended/perl/libtimedate-perl_2.35.bb
similarity index 31%
rename from meta/recipes-extended/perl/libtimedate-perl_2.30.bb
rename to meta/recipes-extended/perl/libtimedate-perl_2.35.bb
index 028630ba90..269eff7cb4 100644
--- a/meta/recipes-extended/perl/libtimedate-perl_2.30.bb
+++ b/meta/recipes-extended/perl/libtimedate-perl_2.35.bb
@@ -1,20 +1,35 @@
 SUMMARY = "Perl modules useful for manipulating date and time information"
+DESCRIPTION = "This is the perl5 TimeDate distribution. It \
+               requires perl version 5.003 or later."
 HOMEPAGE = "https://metacpan.org/release/TimeDate"
-DESCRIPTION = "This is the perl5 TimeDate distribution. It requires perl version 5.003 or later."
+BUGTRACKER = "https://github.com/cpan-authors/TimeDate/issues"
 SECTION = "libs"
 # You can redistribute it and/or modify it under the same terms as Perl itself.
 LICENSE = "Artistic-1.0 OR GPL-1.0-or-later"
-LIC_FILES_CHKSUM = "file://README;beginline=21;md5=576b7cb41e5e821501a01ed66f0f9d9e"
+LIC_FILES_CHKSUM = "file://LICENSE;md5=785dacdd4fe95b580e7b020d087ce54e"
 
-SRC_URI = "${CPAN_MIRROR}/authors/id/G/GB/GBARR/TimeDate-${PV}.tar.gz"
+SRC_URI = "${CPAN_MIRROR}/authors/id/A/AT/ATOOMIC/TimeDate-${PV}.tar.gz"
+SRC_URI[sha256sum] = "baddd0306ae2e86e9ec28d3de5439e514643e80b3735e43bd0fbb426d73304de"
 
 S = "${UNPACKDIR}/TimeDate-${PV}"
 
 inherit cpan ptest-perl
 
-BBCLASSEXTEND = "native"
-
-RDEPENDS:${PN} += "perl-module-carp perl-module-exporter perl-module-strict perl-module-time-local"
-RDEPENDS:${PN}-ptest += "perl-module-test-more perl-module-utf8"
+RDEPENDS:${PN} += "\
+    perl-module-carp \
+    perl-module-exporter \
+    perl-module-posix \
+    perl-module-strict \
+    perl-module-time-local \
+"
+RDEPENDS:${PN}-ptest += "\
+    perl-module-extutils-makemaker \
+    perl-module-extutils-mm-unix \
+    perl-module-file-spec \
+    perl-module-test-more \
+    perl-module-utf8 \
+    perl-module-warnings \
+    tzdata-core \
+"
 
-SRC_URI[sha256sum] = "75bd254871cb5853a6aa0403ac0be270cdd75c9d1b6639f18ecba63c15298e86"
+BBCLASSEXTEND = "native"
-- 
